%erg v1
Title: Add erg tag/untag CLI commands for mutable tag management
Created: 2026-05-11
Author: MinhHaDuong

--- log ---
2026-05-11T21:00Z MinhHaDuong created

--- body ---
## Context

Tags are currently write-once: set when a ticket is created, never changed
by the binary. There is no CLI to add or remove a tag after creation.
Downstream consumers (IDH pick-ticket, erg ready) need a way to mark
tickets with state tags like `claimed` that must be set and cleared during
a ticket's lifecycle.

The motivating use case is replacing branch-as-claim heuristics with an
explicit `Tag: claimed` header, but the interface is general-purpose —
any valid tag can be added or removed.

## Design

Two new subcommands:

```
erg tag   <id> <tagname>    # add Tag: <tagname> to headers, log the action
erg untag <id> <tagname>    # remove Tag: <tagname> from headers, log the action
```

Behavior:
- `erg tag` inserts a `Tag: <tagname>` header line (after the last existing
  header, before the blank line). Appends log: `{ts} {actor} tag {tagname}`.
  Idempotent: if the tag already exists, log "already tagged" and exit 0.
- `erg untag` removes the matching `Tag: <tagname>` header line.
  Appends log: `{ts} {actor} untag {tagname}`. Idempotent: if absent,
  log "not tagged" and exit 0.
- Tag values are validated against the closed set (spec rule 5).
  The closed set is extended with `claimed` as part of this ticket.
- `erg close` should auto-untag `claimed` (a closed+claimed ticket is
  nonsensical).

## Exit criteria

1. `erg tag 0001 needs-human` adds a `Tag: needs-human` header and a log line.
2. `erg untag 0001 needs-human` removes that header and appends a log line.
3. Both commands reject values outside the closed tag set.
4. Both commands are idempotent (exit 0 on no-op).
5. `erg close` removes any `Tag: claimed` header.
6. `claimed` is a valid tag value (added to the closed set).
